/-!
# The general affine case of Stacks 053R

Let `A ⊆ B` be a finitely generated extension of domains, let `g ∈ B` be invertible in the
generic fibre `K ⊗[A] B`, and let `𝔭` be a prime of `A` whose fibre has dimension at most that of
the generic fibre. This file proves that the zero locus of `g` in the fibre over `𝔭` is a union
of irreducible components of that fibre, **with no Noetherian hypothesis**.

The Noetherian case is
`Stacks.Divisors.zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_isNoetherianRing`. The last
paragraph of the source's proof reduces the general case to it by descending the whole situation
to a finitely generated `ℤ`-algebra, and that descent is what this file carries out.

Write `B = A[X_1, …, X_n]/I`. Condition (2) gives `g · h = a` in `B` for some `h ∈ B` and some
nonzero `a ∈ A` — the image of `g` in the localization of `B` at the nonzero elements of `A` is a
unit, so it is a fraction. Lift `g` and `h` to polynomials and choose, by
`MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_map_comap_eq`, a subalgebra `A₀ ⊆ A` of finite type over `ℤ`
containing `a` and the coefficients of those two polynomials, and for which `I ∩ A₀[X]` already
generates `I` over both residue fields `κ(⊥)` and `κ(𝔭)`. Let `B₀ ⊆ B` be the `A₀`-subalgebra
generated by the images of the variables, i.e. the range of `A₀[X] → B`. Then:

* `B₀` is of finite type over the Noetherian ring `A₀`, hence Noetherian, so the Noetherian case
  applies to `A₀ ⊆ B₀`;
* `g`, `h` and `a` all live in `B₀` resp. `A₀`, so `g` is invertible in the generic fibre of `B₀`
  by `Stacks.Divisors.isUnit_genericFiber_of_mul_eq_algebraMap`;
* both fibres of `B₀` are the corresponding fibres of `B`, by
  `Stacks.Divisors.tensorRangeEquiv`, and the Krull dimension of a fibre is insensitive to an
  extension of the residue field by
  `Stacks.Divisors.ringKrullDim_tensor_eq_of_fieldExtension`, so the dimension inequality
  descends as well.

The Noetherian case therefore applies at `A₀ ⊆ B₀`, and its conclusion is carried to `A ⊆ B`
along the comparison map `κ(𝔭₀) ⊗[A₀] B₀ → κ(𝔭) ⊗[A] B` of
`Stacks.Divisors.exists_flat_fiber_comparison`. That map is flat — a base change along the field
extension `κ(𝔭₀) → κ(𝔭)` followed by an isomorphism — so its map on spectra lifts
generalizations and
`AlgebraicGeometry.eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_preimage_of_generalizingMap` transports the
shape of the conclusion.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Divisors.tensorRangeEquiv`: the comparison `L ⊗[A₀] B₀ ≃ L ⊗[A] B` of a fibre of the
  descended algebra with the corresponding fibre of the original one.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Divisors.ker_eq_comap_map_of_comp`: the kernel of `A₀[X] → B` is the contraction of the
  kernel of `A[X] → B`.
* `Stacks.Divisors.tensorRangeEquiv_tmul`,
  `Stacks.Divisors.tensorRangeEquiv_algebraMap`: the value of
  `Stacks.Divisors.tensorRangeEquiv` on a pure tensor, and on the image of an element of `B₀`;
  it is the identity on elements, which is what makes `g` correspond to `g`.
* `Stacks.Divisors.exists_mul_eq_algebraMap_of_isUnit_genericFiber`: condition (2) of the source
  made explicit — invertibility in the generic fibre produces `h ∈ B` and `0 ≠ a ∈ A` with
  `g · h = a`.
* `Stacks.Divisors.isUnit_genericFiber_of_mul_eq_algebraMap`: the converse — such a
  factorisation makes `g` invertible in the generic fibre.
* `Stacks.Divisors.ringKrullDim_tensor_eq_of_fieldExtension`: the Krull dimension of a fibre of a
  finite type algebra does not change under an extension of the residue field.
* `Stacks.Divisors.exists_flat_fiber_comparison`: the flat comparison map between the fibre over
  a residue field and the fibre over an extension of it.
* `Stacks.Divisors.zeroLocus_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_flat`: the shape of the
  conclusion of Stacks 053R travels along a flat ring map.
* `Stacks.Divisors.zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents`: **the general affine case of
  Stacks 053R, in algebraic form.**
* `Stacks.Divisors.fiber_preimage_zeroLocus_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents`: **the general
  affine case of Stacks 053R**, for the scheme-theoretic fibre of `Spec B ⟶ Spec A`.

## Implementation notes

The descended algebra `B₀` is realised as `restriction.range`, the range of the `A₀`-algebra map
`A₀[X] → B`, rather than as a quotient of `A₀[X]`; this makes its elements literally elements of
`B`, so that `g ∈ B₀` is a membership statement and no transport is needed to compare `g` with
its descent. `Stacks.Divisors.tensorRangeEquiv` is the resulting comparison of fibres, assembled
from `MvPolynomial.tensorQuotientComapAlgEquiv` by identifying `B₀` with `A₀[X] / (I ∩ A₀[X])`.

Two features of the descent are forced by `A₀` being a *subalgebra* of `A`, so that the ring
`↥A₀` carries `Subalgebra`-specific instances alongside the `Algebra`-derived ones, definitionally
equal to them but not syntactically.

* The residue field extension `κ(𝔭₀) → κ(𝔭)` cannot be introduced as
  `Ideal.isScalarTower_residueField`: `IsScalarTower` takes its three `SMul` instances as
  arguments, and at `↥A₀` the instance `SMul ↥A₀ κ(𝔭)` that instance search finds is not the one
  that lemma's statement mentions, so the resulting term is not the instance
  `Stacks.Divisors.ringKrullDim_tensor_eq_of_fieldExtension` asks for. The tower is therefore
  built by `IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq` *with no type ascription*, which produces it with the
  `SMul` instances derived from the ambient `Algebra` instances — exactly the consumer's form.
* Every rewrite that would have to see through those instances is performed in a separate theorem
  stated for abstract rings, where there is nothing to see through, and the concrete instance is
  reached by a single application. This is what
  `Stacks.Divisors.tensorRangeEquiv_algebraMap`,
  `Stacks.Divisors.exists_flat_fiber_comparison` and
  `Stacks.Divisors.zeroLocus_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_flat` are for; inlining any of
  them makes the descent exceed the elaboration budget.

Elements produced by the descent — the descended `g`, `h` and `a` — are introduced by `obtain`
from an existential rather than by `let`, together with the equation naming their image. A
`let`-bound witness is definitionally transparent but *syntactically* opaque, so `rw` cannot see
through it; carrying the equation instead keeps every rewrite syntactic.

The algebra structure of `κ(𝔭) ⊗[A] B` over `B` is `Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra`, enabled
here by `attribute [local instance]`; enable it the same way to use these statements. The two
`MvPolynomial` local instances of
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.FinitePresentation.FiniteTypeDescent` are enabled the same way for the
one lemma that needs them, and `Ideal.residueFieldAlgebra` for the descent itself.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 053R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/053R)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry

open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

namespace Stacks.Divisors

/-! ### Comparing a fibre of the descended algebra with a fibre of the original -/

/-- The kernel of a presentation `A₀[X] → B` obtained by restricting a presentation
`A[X] → B` to a subring `A₀ ⊆ A` is the contraction of the kernel of the latter. -/
public theorem ker_eq_comap_map_of_comp
    {R₀ R T : Type*} [CommRing R₀] [CommRing R] [CommRing T]
    [Algebra R₀ R] [Algebra R T] [Algebra R₀ T] [IsScalarTower R₀ R T]
    {σ : Type*} (presentation : MvPolynomial σ R →ₐ[R] T)
    (restriction : MvPolynomial σ R₀ →ₐ[R₀] T)
    (hrestriction : ∀ polynomial, restriction polynomial =
      presentation (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R₀ R) polynomial)) :
    RingHom.ker restriction =
      (RingHom.ker presentation).comap (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R₀ R)) := by
  ext polynomial
  simp only [RingHom.mem_ker, Ideal.mem_comap, hrestriction]

/-- **The fibres of the descended algebra are the fibres of the original one.** Let
`presentation : A[X] → B` be a surjection, let `restriction : A₀[X] → B` be its restriction to a
subring `A₀ ⊆ A`, and let `L` be an `A`-algebra for which the descent identity of
`MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_map_comap_eq` holds. Then `L ⊗[A₀] B₀ ≃ L ⊗[A] B`, where
`B₀ = restriction.range`. -/
public noncomputable def tensorRangeEquiv
    {R₀ R T L : Type*} [CommRing R₀] [CommRing R] [CommRing T] [CommRing L]
    [Algebra R₀ R] [Algebra R T] [Algebra R₀ T] [IsScalarTower R₀ R T]
    [Algebra R L] [Algebra R₀ L] [IsScalarTower R₀ R L]
    {σ : Type*} (presentation : MvPolynomial σ R →ₐ[R] T)
    (hsurjective : Function.Surjective presentation)
    (restriction : MvPolynomial σ R₀ →ₐ[R₀] T)
    (hrestriction : ∀ polynomial, restriction polynomial =
      presentation (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R₀ R) polynomial))
    (hdescent : ((RingHom.ker presentation).comap
        (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R₀ R))).map
          ((MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R L)).comp
            (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R₀ R))) =
        (RingHom.ker presentation).map (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R L))) :
    L ⊗[R₀] restriction.range ≃ₐ[L] L ⊗[R] T :=
  (Algebra.TensorProduct.congr (AlgEquiv.refl (R := L))
      (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective restriction.rangeRestrict_surjective).symm).trans
    ((Algebra.TensorProduct.congr (AlgEquiv.refl (R := L))
      (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq R₀
        ((AlgHom.ker_rangeRestrict restriction).trans
          (ker_eq_comap_map_of_comp presentation restriction hrestriction)))).trans
      ((MvPolynomial.tensorQuotientComapAlgEquiv _ hdescent).trans
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.congr (AlgEquiv.refl (R := L))
          (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective hsurjective))))

end Stacks.Divisors

section MvPolynomialInstances

attribute [local instance] Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra
attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.algebraMvPolynomial
attribute [local instance] isScalarTower_quotient_mvPolynomial

namespace Stacks.Divisors

/-- `Stacks.Divisors.tensorRangeEquiv` is the identity on elements: it sends `s ⊗ x` with
`x ∈ B₀ ⊆ B` to `s ⊗ x`. This is what makes a descended element correspond to itself. -/
public theorem tensorRangeEquiv_tmul
    {R₀ R T L : Type*} [CommRing R₀] [CommRing R] [CommRing T] [CommRing L]
    [Algebra R₀ R] [Algebra R T] [Algebra R₀ T] [IsScalarTower R₀ R T]
    [Algebra R L] [Algebra R₀ L] [IsScalarTower R₀ R L]
    {σ : Type*} (presentation : MvPolynomial σ R →ₐ[R] T)
    (hsurjective : Function.Surjective presentation)
    (restriction : MvPolynomial σ R₀ →ₐ[R₀] T)
    (hrestriction : ∀ polynomial, restriction polynomial =
      presentation (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R₀ R) polynomial))
    (hdescent : ((RingHom.ker presentation).comap
        (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R₀ R))).map
          ((MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R L)).comp
            (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R₀ R))) =
        (RingHom.ker presentation).map (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R L)))
    (scalar : L) (element : restriction.range) :
    tensorRangeEquiv presentation hsurjective restriction hrestriction hdescent
        (scalar ⊗ₜ[R₀] element) = scalar ⊗ₜ[R] (element : T) := by
  obtain ⟨polynomial, rfl⟩ := restriction.rangeRestrict_surjective element
  simp only [tensorRangeEquiv, AlgEquiv.trans_apply, Algebra.TensorProduct.congr_apply,
    Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul, AlgEquiv.coe_toAlgHom]
  rw [Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective_symm_apply]
  simp only [Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq_mk]
  rw [MvPolynomial.tensorQuotientComapAlgEquiv_tmul_mk]
  simp only [Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul,
    AlgEquiv.coe_toAlgHom, Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective_mk]
  rw [← hrestriction]
  rfl

/-- `Stacks.Divisors.tensorRangeEquiv` carries the image of an element of `B₀` in the fibre of
`B₀` to the image of that same element of `B` in the fibre of `B`. This is
`Stacks.Divisors.tensorRangeEquiv_tmul` in the form the descent consumes, and it is stated here —
where the rings are still abstract — so that the rewrites it needs are cheap. -/
public theorem tensorRangeEquiv_algebraMap
    {R₀ R T L : Type*} [CommRing R₀] [CommRing R] [CommRing T] [CommRing L]
    [Algebra R₀ R] [Algebra R T] [Algebra R₀ T] [IsScalarTower R₀ R T]
    [Algebra R L] [Algebra R₀ L] [IsScalarTower R₀ R L]
    {σ : Type*} (presentation : MvPolynomial σ R →ₐ[R] T)
    (hsurjective : Function.Surjective presentation)
    (restriction : MvPolynomial σ R₀ →ₐ[R₀] T)
    (hrestriction : ∀ polynomial, restriction polynomial =
      presentation (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R₀ R) polynomial))
    (hdescent : ((RingHom.ker presentation).comap
        (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R₀ R))).map
          ((MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R L)).comp
            (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R₀ R))) =
        (RingHom.ker presentation).map (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R L)))
    (element : restriction.range) :
    tensorRangeEquiv presentation hsurjective restriction hrestriction hdescent
        (algebraMap restriction.range (L ⊗[R₀] restriction.range) element) =
      algebraMap T (L ⊗[R] T) (element : T) := by
  rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.right_algebraMap_apply,
    Algebra.TensorProduct.right_algebraMap_apply, tensorRangeEquiv_tmul]

end Stacks.Divisors

end MvPolynomialInstances

section Fibre

attribute [local instance] Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra

namespace Stacks.Divisors

/-! ### The factorisation produced by invertibility in the generic fibre -/

/-- **Condition (2) of the last paragraph of the proof of Stacks 053R, made explicit.** If the
image of `g ∈ B` in the generic fibre `K ⊗[A] B` is a unit, then `g · h = a` in `B` for some
`h ∈ B` and some nonzero `a ∈ A`: the generic fibre is the localization of `B` at the nonzero
elements of `A`, so a unit there is a fraction with numerator in `B` and denominator in `A`. -/
public theorem exists_mul_eq_algebraMap_of_isUnit_genericFiber
    {R T : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing T] [IsDomain R] [IsDomain T] [Algebra R T] (element : T)
    (hunit : IsUnit (algebraMap T ((⊥ : Ideal R).Fiber T) element)) :
    ∃ scalar : R, scalar ≠ 0 ∧ ∃ multiplier : T,
      element * multiplier = algebraMap R T scalar := by
  obtain ⟨denominator, hdenominator, multiplier, hmultiplier⟩ :=
    (IsLocalization.algebraMap_isUnit_iff (S := (⊥ : Ideal R).Fiber T)
      (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid T (nonZeroDivisors R))).mp hunit
  obtain ⟨scalar, hscalar, rfl⟩ := hdenominator
  exact ⟨scalar, mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_ne_zero.mp hscalar,
    multiplier, hmultiplier.symm⟩

/-- **The converse of `Stacks.Divisors.exists_mul_eq_algebraMap_of_isUnit_genericFiber`.** A
factorisation `g · h = a` with `a` a nonzero element of the domain `A` makes `g` invertible in
the generic fibre `K ⊗[A] B`, because `a` becomes invertible there. This is how condition (2) is
carried down the descent: the factorisation lives in the descended algebra. -/
public theorem isUnit_genericFiber_of_mul_eq_algebraMap
    {R T : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing T] [IsDomain R] [Algebra R T]
    (element multiplier : T) (scalar : R) (hscalar : scalar ≠ 0)
    (heq : element * multiplier = algebraMap R T scalar) :
    IsUnit (algebraMap T ((⊥ : Ideal R).Fiber T) element) := by
  have hnonzero : algebraMap R (⊥ : Ideal R).ResidueField scalar ≠ 0 := fun hzero =>
    hscalar (Ideal.mem_bot.mp (Ideal.algebraMap_residueField_eq_zero.mp hzero))
  have hunit : IsUnit (algebraMap R (⊥ : Ideal R).ResidueField scalar) :=
    isUnit_iff_ne_zero.mpr hnonzero
  refine isUnit_of_mul_isUnit_left (y := algebraMap T ((⊥ : Ideal R).Fiber T) multiplier) ?_
  rw [← map_mul, heq, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R T ((⊥ : Ideal R).Fiber T),
    IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R (⊥ : Ideal R).ResidueField ((⊥ : Ideal R).Fiber T)]
  exact hunit.map (algebraMap (⊥ : Ideal R).ResidueField ((⊥ : Ideal R).Fiber T))

/-- **The dimension of a fibre is unchanged by an extension of the residue field.** For a finite
type `A`-algebra `B` and a tower of fields `k → K` over `A`, the rings `k ⊗[A] B` and `K ⊗[A] B`
have the same Krull dimension. This is Stacks 00P3 applied to the base change along `k → K`. -/
public theorem ringKrullDim_tensor_eq_of_fieldExtension
    {R k K T : Type*} [CommRing R] [Field k] [Field K] [CommRing T]
    [Algebra R k] [Algebra R K] [Algebra k K] [IsScalarTower R k K]
    [Algebra R T] [Algebra.FiniteType R T] :
    ringKrullDim (k ⊗[R] T) = ringKrullDim (K ⊗[R] T) :=
  (Algebra.IsPushout.ringKrullDim_eq k K (k ⊗[R] T) (K ⊗[k] (k ⊗[R] T))).trans
    (ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.cancelBaseChange R k K K T).toRingEquiv)

/-! ### Transport along the comparison map of fibres -/

/-- **The comparison map of two fibres along an extension of the residue field.** Let `k → K` be
an extension of fields over a ring `A₀`, let `C` be an `A₀`-algebra and let the fibre `K ⊗[A₀] C`
be identified with a ring `D`. Then there is a flat ring map `k ⊗[A₀] C → D` carrying the image
of an element of `C` to the image of that element.

It is the base change `k ⊗[A₀] C → K ⊗[A₀] C` along `k → K`, which is flat because `k` is a
field, followed by the given isomorphism. -/
public theorem exists_flat_fiber_comparison
    {R k K C D : Type*} [CommRing R] [Field k] [Field K] [CommRing C] [CommRing D]
    [Algebra R k] [Algebra R K] [Algebra k K] [IsScalarTower R k K] [Algebra R C]
    [Algebra K D] (e : K ⊗[R] C ≃ₐ[K] D) (x : C) :
    ∃ φ : k ⊗[R] C →+* D, φ.Flat ∧
      φ (algebraMap C (k ⊗[R] C) x) = e (algebraMap C (K ⊗[R] C) x) := by
  refine ⟨e.toRingEquiv.toRingHom.comp (Algebra.TensorProduct.map
    (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom R k K) (AlgHom.id R C)).toRingHom, ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact (RingHom.Flat.tensorProductMap (RingHom.Flat.of_isField (Field.toIsField _) _)
      (RingHom.Flat.of_bijective (f := (AlgHom.id R C).toRingHom) Function.bijective_id)).comp
      (RingHom.Flat.of_bijective e.bijective)
  · show e (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom R k K) (AlgHom.id R C)
        (algebraMap C (k ⊗[R] C) x)) = e (algebraMap C (K ⊗[R] C) x)
    rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.right_algebraMap_apply,
      Algebra.TensorProduct.right_algebraMap_apply, Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul, map_one,
      AlgHom.id_apply]

/-- **The shape of the conclusion of Stacks 053R travels along a flat ring map.** If the zero
locus of `x` in `Spec R` is the union of the irreducible components of `Spec R` it contains, and
`φ : R → S` is flat with `φ x = y`, then the zero locus of `y` in `Spec S` is the union of the
irreducible components of `Spec S` it contains: it is the preimage of the zero locus of `x`, and
`Spec φ` lifts generalizations. -/
public theorem zeroLocus_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_flat {R S : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] (φ : R →+* S) (hflat : φ.Flat) (x : R) (y : S) (hxy : φ x = y)
    (hcomponents : (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {x} : Set (PrimeSpectrum R)) =
      ⋃₀ {Z : Set (PrimeSpectrum R) | Z ∈ irreducibleComponents (PrimeSpectrum R) ∧
        Z ⊆ PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {x}}) :
    (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {y} : Set (PrimeSpectrum S)) =
      ⋃₀ {Z : Set (PrimeSpectrum S) | Z ∈ irreducibleComponents (PrimeSpectrum S) ∧
        Z ⊆ PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {y}} := by
  have hpreimage : PrimeSpectrum.comap φ ⁻¹' (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {x}) =
      (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {y} : Set (PrimeSpectrum S)) := by
    rw [PrimeSpectrum.preimage_comap_zeroLocus, Set.image_singleton, hxy]
  rw [← hpreimage]
  exact AlgebraicGeometry.eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_preimage_of_generalizingMap _
    (PrimeSpectrum.continuous_comap _) hflat.generalizingMap_comap _
    (PrimeSpectrum.isClosed_zeroLocus _) hcomponents

end Stacks.Divisors

end Fibre

section Descent

attribute [local instance] Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra
attribute [local instance] Ideal.residueFieldAlgebra

namespace Stacks.Divisors

variable {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain A] [IsDomain B] [Algebra A B]
  [FaithfulSMul A B] [Algebra.FiniteType A B]

/-- **Stacks 053R, the general affine case, in algebraic form.** Let `A ⊆ B` be a finitely
generated extension of domains, let `g ∈ B`, and let `𝔭` be a prime of `A`. Assume that the image
of `g` in `K ⊗[A] B` is a unit, where `K` is the fraction field of `A` (condition (2) of the
source), and that the fibre over `𝔭` has dimension at most that of the generic fibre (the
inequality half of condition (3)). Then the support of `g` in `Spec (κ(𝔭) ⊗[A] B)` is the union
of the irreducible components of that spectrum contained in it.

No Noetherian hypothesis: the situation is descended to a finitely generated `ℤ`-subalgebra
`A₀ ⊆ A`, over which `B₀ ⊆ B` — the range of the restricted presentation `A₀[X] → B` — is of
finite type and therefore Noetherian, so that
`Stacks.Divisors.zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_isNoetherianRing` applies
there; the conclusion is then carried back along the flat comparison map
`κ(𝔭₀) ⊗[A₀] B₀ → κ(𝔭) ⊗[A] B`. -/
public theorem zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents (g : B) (p : PrimeSpectrum A)
    (hgeneric : IsUnit (algebraMap B ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B) g))
    (hdim : ringKrullDim (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) ≤
      ringKrullDim ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B)) :
    (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {algebraMap B (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) g} :
        Set (PrimeSpectrum (p.asIdeal.Fiber B))) =
      ⋃₀ {Z : Set (PrimeSpectrum (p.asIdeal.Fiber B)) |
        Z ∈ irreducibleComponents (PrimeSpectrum (p.asIdeal.Fiber B)) ∧
        Z ⊆ PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {algebraMap B (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) g}} := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨a, ha, h, hah⟩ := exists_mul_eq_algebraMap_of_isUnit_genericFiber g hgeneric
  obtain ⟨numVars, presentation, hsurjective⟩ :=
    Algebra.FiniteType.iff_quotient_mvPolynomial''.mp (inferInstance : Algebra.FiniteType A B)
  obtain ⟨gPoly, hgPoly⟩ := hsurjective g
  obtain ⟨hPoly, hhPoly⟩ := hsurjective h
  obtain ⟨A₀, hA₀adjoin, hA₀fg, hA₀range, hgenericDescent, hfiberDescent⟩ :=
    MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_map_comap_eq (RingHom.ker presentation)
      ((⊥ : Ideal A).ResidueField) p.asIdeal.ResidueField {gPoly, hPoly} (Set.toFinite _)
      (Algebra.adjoin ℤ {a}) (Subalgebra.fg_def.mpr ⟨{a}, Set.finite_singleton _, rfl⟩)
  have haA₀ : a ∈ A₀ := hA₀adjoin (Algebra.subset_adjoin (Set.mem_singleton a))
  have : Algebra.FiniteType ℤ A₀ := (Subalgebra.fg_iff_finiteType A₀).mp hA₀fg
  let restriction : MvPolynomial (Fin numVars) A₀ →ₐ[A₀] B :=
    (presentation.restrictScalars A₀).comp (MvPolynomial.mapAlgHom (Algebra.ofId A₀ A))
  have hrestriction (polynomial : MvPolynomial (Fin numVars) A₀) :
      restriction polynomial =
        presentation (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A) polynomial) := rfl
  obtain ⟨gPoly₀, hgPoly₀⟩ := hA₀range gPoly (by simp)
  obtain ⟨hPoly₀, hhPoly₀⟩ := hA₀range hPoly (by simp)
  obtain ⟨g₀, hg₀⟩ : ∃ x : restriction.range, (x : B) = g :=
    ⟨⟨g, (AlgHom.mem_range restriction).mpr
      ⟨gPoly₀, by rw [hrestriction, hgPoly₀]; exact hgPoly⟩⟩, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨h₀, hh₀⟩ : ∃ x : restriction.range, (x : B) = h :=
    ⟨⟨h, (AlgHom.mem_range restriction).mpr
      ⟨hPoly₀, by rw [hrestriction, hhPoly₀]; exact hhPoly⟩⟩, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨a₀, ha₀⟩ : ∃ x : A₀, (x : A) = a := ⟨⟨a, haA₀⟩, rfl⟩
  have ha₀ne : a₀ ≠ 0 := fun hzero => ha (by rw [← ha₀, hzero]; simp)
  have heq₀ : g₀ * h₀ = algebraMap A₀ restriction.range a₀ :=
    Subtype.ext (by
      show (g₀ : B) * (h₀ : B) = algebraMap A B (a₀ : A)
      rw [hg₀, hh₀, ha₀, hah])
  have : Algebra.FiniteType A₀ restriction.range :=
    Algebra.FiniteType.of_surjective restriction.rangeRestrict
      restriction.rangeRestrict_surjective
  have : IsNoetherianRing A₀ := Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing ℤ _
  have : IsNoetherianRing restriction.range := Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing A₀ _
  have : FaithfulSMul A₀ restriction.range :=
    (faithfulSMul_iff_algebraMap_injective _ _).mpr fun x y hxy =>
      Subtype.ext (FaithfulSMul.algebraMap_injective A B
        (show algebraMap A B (x : A) = algebraMap A B (y : A) from congrArg Subtype.val hxy))
  have : FaithfulSMul A₀ A :=
    (faithfulSMul_iff_algebraMap_injective _ _).mpr fun x y hxy =>
      Subtype.ext (show (x : A) = (y : A) from hxy)
  let base₀ : PrimeSpectrum A₀ := PrimeSpectrum.comap (algebraMap A₀ A) p
  have : p.asIdeal.LiesOver base₀.asIdeal := ⟨rfl⟩
  -- The two residue field extensions, as scalar towers. These must be produced *without* a type
  -- ascription; see the implementation notes.
  have := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq (R := A₀) (S := base₀.asIdeal.ResidueField)
    (A := p.asIdeal.ResidueField) fun x => by
      simp [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra, Ideal.ResidueField.map_algebraMap,
        IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A₀ A p.asIdeal.ResidueField]
  have := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq (R := A₀) (S := (⊥ : Ideal A₀).ResidueField)
    (A := (⊥ : Ideal A).ResidueField) fun x => by
      simp [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra, Ideal.ResidueField.map_algebraMap,
        IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A₀ A (⊥ : Ideal A).ResidueField]
  -- The dimension inequality descends: a fibre does not change dimension when the residue field
  -- is enlarged, and both fibres of `B₀` are the corresponding fibres of `B`.
  have hfiberField : ringKrullDim (base₀.asIdeal.ResidueField ⊗[A₀] restriction.range) =
      ringKrullDim (p.asIdeal.ResidueField ⊗[A₀] restriction.range) :=
    ringKrullDim_tensor_eq_of_fieldExtension (R := A₀)
      (k := base₀.asIdeal.ResidueField) (K := p.asIdeal.ResidueField) (T := restriction.range)
  have hbotField : ringKrullDim ((⊥ : Ideal A₀).ResidueField ⊗[A₀] restriction.range) =
      ringKrullDim ((⊥ : Ideal A).ResidueField ⊗[A₀] restriction.range) :=
    ringKrullDim_tensor_eq_of_fieldExtension (R := A₀)
      (k := (⊥ : Ideal A₀).ResidueField) (K := (⊥ : Ideal A).ResidueField)
      (T := restriction.range)
  have hfiberRange : ringKrullDim (p.asIdeal.ResidueField ⊗[A₀] restriction.range) =
      ringKrullDim (p.asIdeal.ResidueField ⊗[A] B) :=
    ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv (tensorRangeEquiv presentation hsurjective restriction
      hrestriction hfiberDescent).toRingEquiv
  have hbotRange : ringKrullDim ((⊥ : Ideal A).ResidueField ⊗[A₀] restriction.range) =
      ringKrullDim ((⊥ : Ideal A).ResidueField ⊗[A] B) :=
    ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv (tensorRangeEquiv presentation hsurjective restriction
      hrestriction hgenericDescent).toRingEquiv
  have hcomponents₀ := zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_isNoetherianRing
    g₀ base₀ (isUnit_genericFiber_of_mul_eq_algebraMap g₀ h₀ a₀ ha₀ne heq₀)
    ((hfiberField.trans hfiberRange).le.trans (hdim.trans (hbotField.trans hbotRange).ge))
  -- Transport along the flat comparison map of the two fibres over `𝔭₀` and `𝔭`.
  obtain ⟨comparison, hcomparisonFlat, hcomparisonValue⟩ :=
    exists_flat_fiber_comparison (R := A₀) (k := base₀.asIdeal.ResidueField)
      (K := p.asIdeal.ResidueField)
      (tensorRangeEquiv presentation hsurjective restriction hrestriction hfiberDescent) g₀
  have hvalue := tensorRangeEquiv_algebraMap presentation hsurjective restriction hrestriction
    hfiberDescent g₀
  rw [hg₀] at hvalue
  exact zeroLocus_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_flat comparison hcomparisonFlat _ _
    (hcomparisonValue.trans hvalue) hcomponents₀

/-- **Stacks 053R for an affine morphism, in general.** Let `A ⊆ B` be a finitely generated
extension of domains, let `g ∈ B` be invertible in the generic fibre `K ⊗[A] B`, and let `𝔭` be a
prime of `A` whose fibre of `Spec B ⟶ Spec A` has dimension at most that of the generic fibre.
Then the part of the fibre over `𝔭` lying in the zero locus of `g` is the union of the
irreducible components of that fibre contained in it.

This is `Stacks.Divisors.zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents` read through the affine
fibre dictionary of `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FibreDimension.AffineFibre`. -/
public theorem fiber_preimage_zeroLocus_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents (g : B)
    (p : PrimeSpectrum A)
    (hgeneric : IsUnit (algebraMap B ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B) g))
    (hdim : topologicalKrullDim ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber p) ≤
      topologicalKrullDim ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber
        (genericPoint (Spec (CommRingCat.of A))))) :
    (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiberι p ⁻¹'
        (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {g} : Set (PrimeSpectrum B)) =
      ⋃₀ {C : Set ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber p) |
        C ∈ irreducibleComponents ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiber p) ∧
        C ⊆ (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))).fiberι p ⁻¹'
          (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {g} : Set (PrimeSpectrum B))} := by
  have hdim' : ringKrullDim (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) ≤
      ringKrullDim ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B) :=
    (topologicalKrullDim_fiber_specMap_eq A B p).ge.trans
      (hdim.trans (topologicalKrullDim_fiber_specMap_genericPoint_eq A B).le)
  refine (fiberSpecHomeo A B p).symm.eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_image ?_
    (zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents g p hgeneric hdim')
  rw [← fiberSpecHomeo_image_preimage_zeroLocus A B p g, Set.image_image]
  simp

